{"File":"/Users/jps/Dropbox/simula agulhas/project_report.tex","LineNumber":114,"LineContent":"The simulator supports three lattice geometries (square, triangular, honeycomb); \\textbf{seven} external-field modes: static; First-Order Reversal Curve (FORC) mode with sat/reversal field parameter control; pulse with explicit timing (delay $\\Delta t$ $\\to$ field for $t_{\\mathrm{pulse}}$ $\\to$ zero field until equilibrium, with the legacy saturation/plateau criterion if $t_{\\mathrm{pulse}}$ is not given); five-segment hysteresis ($0 \\to +B \\to 0 \\to -B \\to 0 \\to +B$) with linear or log-symmetric spacing; sinusoidal field; and step modes \\code{step\\_pos} ($B{=}0$ for $\\Delta t$, then field kept on) and \\code{step\\_neg} (field from $t{=}0$, removed at $\\Delta t$). Additionally, a sinusoidal decaying demagnetization procedure (\\code{--demag on}) can be enabled before any field mode. It also supports periodic boundary conditions with lattice images; real-time monitoring of the alignment order parameter $S \\in [0,1]$; a real-equilibrium criterion (small angular velocity \\emph{and} small mean torque) for pulse/step modes; optional GPU backend through CuPy; MP4 video export, summary images, and CSV time series $(t, B, M, S)$; magnetic-domain visualization through halo coloring; a precomputed dipolar tensor (V40); and performance instrumentation."}
