176: \subsection{Phase 6 --- from tool to research (18/06 and 04--05/07)}
177: 
178: With the instrument mature, the focus shifted to science:
179: 
180: \begin{enumerate}
181: \item \textbf{Literature review}, detailed in Section~\ref{sec:research}, identifying the gap and study design;
182: \item \textbf{Publication strategy}, including ACS journals, the CAPES agreement, and high-impact alternatives;
183: \item \textbf{\code{--make\_images} (V39)}: it was found that, even without \code{--video}, the program unconditionally generated 4--5 summary PNG images per run. This cost is negligible in large arrays, but dominant in small arrays used for sweeps. The new parameter suppresses all image generation while preserving data CSVs, with a measured speedup of $\sim 3\times$ in small runs (2.03~s $\to$ 0.65~s for an $8\times8$ array);
184: \item \textbf{Campaign infrastructure}: the scripts \code{damping\_sweep.py} (orchestration of damping~$\times$~\emph{seed}~$\times$~geometry sweeps, calling the simulator programmatically) and \code{damping\_sweep\_analysis.py} (full statistical analysis), both validated end to end (Section~\ref{sec:campaign});
185: \item \textbf{Performance optimizations implemented (04/07)}: the precomputed dipolar tensor (\textbf{V40}) and campaign parallelization with incremental \emph{manifest} and resume support (\code{damping\_sweep} V02). Details and measurements are in Section~\ref{sec:improvements}. The measured V40 speedup is \textbf{35--45$\times$} per run, reducing the full campaign from $\sim$7--8~h to $\sim$15~min on a single core;
186: \item \textbf{New field protocols and refinements (V41--V45)}: hysteresis with log-symmetric spacing; pulse with explicit timing ($\Delta t$ + $t_{\mathrm{pulse}}$ + torque equilibrium); step modes \code{step\_pos}/\code{step\_neg}; \code{--t\_sim\_full} flag (run to the end without early stopping); halos also in the comparison figure (V43); a two-line live progress panel (V44); and hysteresis video with a dual progress panel (V45).
187: \item \textbf{Layout, terminal updates, and translations (V46--V66)}: docstring alignment (V46); autoscale parameter \code{--hyst\_autoscale} (V47); bugfixes and autoscale options (V48); HUD-needle overlap resolution and signed field bar updates (V49); progress bar English translation alongside a three-line console print layout (V50); HUD legend layout alignment alongside a constant-length field arrow position update (V51); full translation of all remaining terminal console prints and confirmations to English (V52); circular direction dial and sign indicator arrow next to the horizontal field bar updates (V53); terminal banner code version and developer metadata addition (V54); HUD direction dial arrow scaling with the removal of the sign indicator next to the bar (V55); HUD direction dial arrow scaling minimum length calibration (V56); HUD direction dial redesigned as a bold filled arrow using \code{FancyArrow} (V57); HUD direction dial bold arrow homothetic scaling to preserve aspect ratio (V58); random per-needle damping noise support (V59); full translation of all CLI arguments and help text to English (V60); translation of Section 4 plotting label strings to English (V61); translation of the image suppression warning to English (V62); performance optimizations to the integration loop (V63); alignment of sweep files (V64); full translation of all sweep scripts to English (V65); and redesign of the HUD external field intensity bar to grow bidirectionally from center for positive/negative fields and zero at zero field (V66).
188: \item \textbf{FORC protocol implementation (V67--V69)}: introduction of the First-Order Reversal Curve (FORC) field mode (\code{forc}) with saturation/reversal field parameter control (\code{--forc\_Br}, \code{--forc\_t\_sat}, \code{--forc\_t\_rev}), real-time dual-panel video monitoring of the minor reversal loop, and automated export to \code{forc\_curve.csv}. Added \code{--forc\_sweep} choices to filter branch tracking.
189: \item \textbf{Sinusoidal Demagnetization (V70)}: implementation of a pre-treatment sinusoidal alternating field demagnetization (AFD) procedure (\code{--demag on}), sweeping the field from $+B_{\mathrm{ext}}$ to zero, decaying 30\% per cycle, at a configurable frequency \code{--demag\_freq}.
190: \end{enumerate}
