{"File":"/Users/jps/Dropbox/simula agulhas/project_report.tex","LineNumber":248,"LineContent":"\\caption{Pilot: avalanche exponent $\\tau$ (MLE, avalanches aggregated across 3 seeds) by geometry and quality factor. ``---'' indicates insufficient statistics ($n_{\\mathrm{tail}} \u003c$ minimum) in the shortened pilot cycle.}"}
{"File":"/Users/jps/Dropbox/simula agulhas/project_report.tex","LineNumber":266,"LineContent":"\\caption{Central test of the study (pilot): avalanche power-law exponent $\\tau$ as a function of the quality factor $Q$, by geometry. The systematic increase of $\\tau$ with $Q$, if confirmed in the full campaign with adequate statistics, is the candidate signature that the universality class depends on the damping regime under dipolar coupling.}"}
{"File":"/Users/jps/Dropbox/simula agulhas/project_report.tex","LineNumber":292,"LineContent":"\\textbf{Question.} Does the quality factor $Q$ control the universality class of avalanches and the shape of the hysteresis loop under complete dipolar coupling? Does the answer depend on geometry?"}
