{"File":"/Users/jps/Dropbox/simula agulhas/project_report.tex","LineNumber":114,"LineContent":"The simulator supports three lattice geometries (square, triangular, honeycomb); \\textbf{seven} external-field modes: static; First-Order Reversal Curve (FORC) mode with sat/reversal field parameter control and a constant sweep rate option; pulse with explicit timing (delay $\\Delta t$ $\\to$ field for $t_{\\mathrm{pulse}}$ $\\to$ zero field until equilibrium, with the legacy saturation/plateau criterion if $t_{\\mathrm{pulse}}$ is not given); five-segment hysteresis ($0 \\to +B \\to 0 \\to -B \\to 0 \\to +B$) with linear or log-symmetric spacing; sinusoidal field; and step modes \\code{step\\_pos} ($B{=}0$ for $\\Delta t$, then field kept on) and \\code{step\\_neg} (field from $t{=}0$, removed at $\\Delta t$). Additionally, a sinusoidal decaying demagnetization procedure (\\code{--demag on}) can be enabled before any field mode. It also supports periodic boundary conditions with lattice images; real-time monitoring of the alignment order parameter $S \\in [0,1]$; a real-equilibrium criterion (small angular velocity \\emph{and} small mean torque) for pulse/step modes; optional GPU backend through CuPy; MP4 video export, summary images, and CSV time series $(t, B, M, S)$; magnetic-domain visualization through halo coloring; a precomputed dipolar tensor (V40); and performance instrumentation."}
{"File":"/Users/jps/Dropbox/simula agulhas/project_report.tex","LineNumber":189,"LineContent":"\\item \\textbf{Sinusoidal Demagnetization (V70)}: initial implementation of a pre-treatment sinusoidal alternating field demagnetization (AFD) procedure (\\code{--demag on}), sweeping the field from $+B_{\\mathrm{ext}}$ to zero, decaying 30\\% per cycle, at a configurable frequency \\code{--demag\\_freq} (later replaced in V72 by an isotropic biaxial rotational protocol);"}
{"File":"/Users/jps/Dropbox/simula agulhas/project_report.tex","LineNumber":191,"LineContent":"\\item \\textbf{Biaxial Rotational Demagnetization (V72)}: replaced the uniaxial sinusoidal decaying field (AFD) with a biaxial rotational demagnetization protocol (Method A from \\code{compass\\_sim\\_protocol\\_notes.md}), where the field rotates in the $xy$-plane while decaying linearly to zero, providing an isotropic randomized demagnetized state ($S \\to 0$);"}
{"File":"/Users/jps/Dropbox/simula agulhas/project_report.tex","LineNumber":193,"LineContent":"\\item \\textbf{Simulated Thermal Annealing Demagnetization (V74)}: implemented Method B (linear sweep with decaying simulated thermal annealing white noise torque) as an alternative pre-treatment demagnetization protocol, and introduced the temperature scaling parameter \\code{--demag\\_temp};"}
{"File":"/Users/jps/Dropbox/simula agulhas/project_report.tex","LineNumber":194,"LineContent":"\\item \\textbf{Multi-Stage Progress Bar (V75)}: divided the command-line progress bar output into two sequential phases (Demagnetization and Simulation/Measurement) with phase-specific labels, percentages, step counts, and local physical timers."}
{"File":"/Users/jps/Dropbox/simula agulhas/project_report.tex","LineNumber":459,"LineContent":"\\code{--demag} \u0026 \\code{off} \u0026 --- \u0026 Demagnetization protocol (\\code{off}, \\code{on}/\\code{rotational}, \\code{anneal}; V70--V74). \\\\"}
{"File":"/Users/jps/Dropbox/simula agulhas/project_report.tex","LineNumber":460,"LineContent":"\\code{--demag\\_freq} \u0026 2.0 \u0026 Hz \u0026 Demagnetization sweep frequency / annealing rotation rate (V70--V74). \\\\"}
{"File":"/Users/jps/Dropbox/simula agulhas/project_report.tex","LineNumber":461,"LineContent":"\\code{--demag\\_cycles} \u0026 20 \u0026 --- \u0026 Number of decay cycles for demagnetization (V70--V74). \\\\"}
{"File":"/Users/jps/Dropbox/simula agulhas/project_report.tex","LineNumber":462,"LineContent":"\\code{--demag\\_temp} \u0026 1.0 \u0026 --- \u0026 Noise temperature factor for simulated annealing (Method B) (V74). \\\\"}
{"File":"/Users/jps/Dropbox/simula agulhas/project_report.tex","LineNumber":623,"LineContent":"\\medskip\\noindent\\textbf{Demagnetization procedure (V74)} --- Before any field mode is executed, an optional pre-treatment phase can be enabled (\\code{--demag}) with two different physical algorithms (Method A and Method B from \\code{compass\\_sim\\_protocol\\_notes.md}):"}
{"File":"/Users/jps/Dropbox/simula agulhas/project_report.tex","LineNumber":625,"LineContent":"\\item \\textbf{Method A: Biaxial Rotational Demagnetization} (\\code{--demag rotational} or \\code{on}) --- The external field vector rotates continuously in the $xy$-plane while its peak magnitude decays linearly to zero:"}
{"File":"/Users/jps/Dropbox/simula agulhas/project_report.tex","LineNumber":627,"LineContent":"B_x(t) \u0026= B_{\\max} \\cdot \\left(1.0 - \\frac{t}{t_{\\text{demag}}}\\right) \\cdot \\cos(2\\pi \\cdot f_{\\text{demag}} \\cdot t) \\\\"}
{"File":"/Users/jps/Dropbox/simula agulhas/project_report.tex","LineNumber":628,"LineContent":"B_y(t) \u0026= B_{\\max} \\cdot \\left(1.0 - \\frac{t}{t_{\\text{demag}}}\\right) \\cdot \\sin(2\\pi \\cdot f_{\\text{demag}} \\cdot t)"}
{"File":"/Users/jps/Dropbox/simula agulhas/project_report.tex","LineNumber":630,"LineContent":"where $t_{\\text{demag}} = \\code{--demag\\_cycles}/\\code{--demag\\_freq}$. This forces all needles through a complete angular sweep in the plane, erasing any directional bias and providing a truer isotropic randomized demagnetized state ($S \\to 0$)."}
{"File":"/Users/jps/Dropbox/simula agulhas/project_report.tex","LineNumber":631,"LineContent":"\\item \\textbf{Method B: Linear Sweep with Simulated Thermal Annealing} (\\code{--demag anneal}) --- The external field decays linearly along the primary direction ($\\phi$) without rotation, but we introduce a temporary random thermal white noise torque $\\tau_i^{\\text{thermal}}(t) = \\sigma(t) \\cdot \\eta_i(t)$ acting on each needle. The noise standard deviation decays linearly to zero starting from an initial intensity scaled by the temperature parameter \\code{--demag\\_temp} ($T$) and the reference torque scale $\\tau_{\\text{ref}} = I \\omega_0^2$:"}
{"File":"/Users/jps/Dropbox/simula agulhas/project_report.tex","LineNumber":632,"LineContent":"$$\\sigma(t) = T \\cdot \\tau_{\\text{ref}} \\cdot \\left(1.0 - \\frac{t}{t_{\\text{demag}}}\\right)$$"}
{"File":"/Users/jps/Dropbox/simula agulhas/project_report.tex","LineNumber":636,"LineContent":"# Run a static field simulation after demagnetizing the sample for 20 cycles"}
{"File":"/Users/jps/Dropbox/simula agulhas/project_report.tex","LineNumber":637,"LineContent":"python3 compass.py --N 10 --M 10 --B_ext 0.005 --demag on --t_sim 1.0"}
{"File":"/Users/jps/Dropbox/simula agulhas/project_report.tex","LineNumber":639,"LineContent":"During the demagnetization pre-treatment phase, the physical integration is carried out to prepare the initial configuration of the needles. Data logging in the output CSV files starts recording exactly at $t_{\\mathrm{phys}} = 0.0$ when the demagnetization completes and the primary field mode begins, while video recording (if enabled) captures the entire process starting from the demagnetization phase with a distinct cyan clock progress bar."}
{"File":"/Users/jps/Dropbox/simula agulhas/project_report.tex","LineNumber":641,"LineContent":"\\medskip\\noindent\\textbf{Tips for accelerating demagnetization execution speed:} \\\\"}
{"File":"/Users/jps/Dropbox/simula agulhas/project_report.tex","LineNumber":642,"LineContent":"The total number of integration steps during the demagnetization phase is given by:"}
{"File":"/Users/jps/Dropbox/simula agulhas/project_report.tex","LineNumber":643,"LineContent":"$$\\text{Steps}_{\\text{demag}} = \\frac{t_{\\text{demag}}}{dt} = \\frac{\\code{--demag\\_cycles}}{\\code{--demag\\_freq} \\cdot \\code{--dt\\_factor} \\cdot T_0}$$"}
{"File":"/Users/jps/Dropbox/simula agulhas/project_report.tex","LineNumber":644,"LineContent":"Because $T_0$ (the natural oscillation period of the needles) is very short under typical magnetic fields, the demagnetization phase can require thousands of steps and become slow on the CPU for larger grids. To optimize performance, the following settings are recommended:"}
{"File":"/Users/jps/Dropbox/simula agulhas/project_report.tex","LineNumber":646,"LineContent":"\\item \\textbf{Reduce decay cycles}: Change \\code{--demag\\_cycles} from the default $20$ to $5$ or $10$. This provides ample relaxation while yielding a direct $2\\times$ to $4\\times$ speedup."}
